      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Westmont was originally part of Rancho Sausal Redondo, a 22,458‑acre Mexican land grant awarded on May 20, 1837, to Antonio Ygnacio Avila by Governor Juan Bautista Alvarado.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Westmont,_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Southern Pacific line reached the South Bay by 1869, and the Los Angeles & Redondo Railway opened in 1890, linking Los Angeles with Redondo Beach.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Westmont,_California",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Westmont enjoys a Mediterranean climate (Köppen Csb), with mild winters, occasional rain, and hot, dry summers shaped by coastal proximity and the urban heat island effect.",
